This Agreement is between the person or entity acquiring the license ("you")
and the copyright holder or authorized licensing entity identified as the
licensor in your License Entitlement ("Licensor"). If you accept on behalf of
an entity, you must have authority to bind that entity.

"Software" means the Gesher software and accompanying documentation supplied
with this Agreement, including any source code supplied. "Proprietary Software"
means only those portions of the Software that Licensor is authorized to
license under this Agreement, excluding materials governed by separate
licenses as described in section 7.

"License Entitlement" means an order, license certificate or other written
license confirmation issued or expressly approved by Licensor. It identifies
Licensor and the licensee, the licensed product or edition, the permitted
users, devices or other usage limits, the license duration (including whether
it is perpetual or time-limited), and the agreed fees and payment terms. An
authorized reseller may supply a License Entitlement on Licensor's behalf.

2. Acceptance and payment

To exercise rights under this Agreement, you must first receive and accept
these terms and obtain a valid License Entitlement. Acceptance must be through
an affirmative acceptance process or a signed agreement incorporating these
terms. Merely accessing a repository or downloading files does not establish
acceptance or grant a commercial license under this Agreement.

Gesher is licensed commercially for a fee. You must pay the fees when due under
your License Entitlement. A trial, evaluation or complimentary license exists
only if Licensor expressly grants it in writing, and is limited to its stated
purpose, scope and duration. Possession of source code, an installer or a
license key alone does not establish a valid License Entitlement.

3. License grant

Subject to this Agreement and your License Entitlement, Licensor grants you a
limited, non-exclusive, non-sublicensable and non-transferable license to
install and run the Proprietary Software in the executable form supplied for
end-user use, including scripts supplied for normal operation, for your own
personal use or internal business purposes, within the agreed usage limits and
license duration. Transfers are permitted where expressly authorized by Licensor
or required by applicable law.

You may make copies necessary for authorized installation and operation and
a reasonable number of backup copies, retaining the applicable notices.
Employees and contractors may use the Software on your behalf within your
License Entitlement and subject to this Agreement; they receive no independent
right to distribute it or use it for other customers.

4. Restrictions on Proprietary Software

Except as expressly permitted by this Agreement, your License Entitlement,
separate written authorization from Licensor, or section 7, you must not:

(a) copy, distribute, publish, sell, sublicense, lend, rent, transfer or make
    the Proprietary Software available to third parties, in source or object
