(b) modify, adapt, translate or create derivative works of the Proprietary
    Software, or develop or distribute a fork of it;
(c) make the Proprietary Software available as a hosted service, service
    bureau or shared offering for third parties;
(d) reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the Proprietary Software;
(e) remove or alter copyright, license, trademark or other proprietary notices;
    or
(f) circumvent license or activation controls, use unauthorized license keys,
    share credentials to exceed the licensed scope, or otherwise exceed the
    usage limits in your License Entitlement.

These restrictions do not prevent using ordinary product settings or creating,
running and sharing your own applications and data without distributing the
Proprietary Software. Rights to applications, content and services used with
Gesher must be obtained from their respective rightsholders where required.

