8. Term and termination

Your license lasts for the duration stated in your License Entitlement. A
perpetual license does not expire merely because a support or update period
ends. A time-limited license expires at the end of its agreed term unless
renewed. Renewal, additional fees and any automatic renewal require the terms
agreed with you; this Agreement does not itself establish automatic renewal.

Licensor may terminate the rights granted under this Agreement for a material
breach, including failure to pay fees when due, by written notice identifying
the breach and allowing a reasonable opportunity to cure it where it can be
cured. If it is cured within that opportunity, termination on that ground does
not take effect. Termination remains subject to applicable law.

On expiry or valid termination, you must stop using and remove copies of the
Proprietary Software licensed solely under this Agreement, except for copies
you are legally required to retain, which may not be used for other purposes.
This does not require deletion of your applications or data, or affect rights
preserved by section 7. Payment obligations already accrued and provisions
concerning ownership, restrictions, separate licenses and limits of liability
survive only to the extent relevant after termination.

9. Updates, support and changes to terms

Updates, upgrades, maintenance and support are included only to the extent
